<title>FRANCE: Accor first-half net attrib rises.</title>
<headline>Accor first-half net attrib rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half of 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     104  vs		29</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-exceptional		   568  vs	     451</p>
<p>    Turnover consolidated		   13,840  vs	  15,986</p>
<p>NOTE - The company released the results in a statement  </p>
<p>    Overall result from operations	   441  vs	     479</p>
<p>    Financial result			     161  vs     not given</p>
<p>Note - Excluding the sale of Eurest, sales rose 8.2 percent. Accor said the overall result from operations should come in at around 1.50 billion francs for the whole of 1996, which would be 220 million more than in 1995, and that the net consolidated result should &quot;progress in line with group objectives&quot;.</p>
<p>Accor said it was continuing its strategy of debt reduction and improving its return on capital, as well as a less cyclical and more service-based improvement in growth and profitability.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
